{"name":"Cloudy Today","hex":"#a6a096","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cloudy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Covered with or characterised by clouds.","Not transparent or clear.\n\n Containing pith"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloudy"},{"term":"today","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["On the current day or date.","In the current era; nowadays; these days."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The current day or date.","The 24-hour period beginning at 5 or 6 a.m. or sunrise of the current day."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/today"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cloud","blocks":[{"text":"In meteorology, a cloud is an aerosol consisting of a visible mass of miniature liquid droplets, ice crystals, or other particles, suspended in the atmosphere of a planetary body or similar space. Water, primarily, comprises the droplets and crystals. On Earth, clouds are formed as a result of saturation of the air when it is cooled to its dew point, or when it gains sufficient moisture, usually in the form of water vapor, from an adjacent source to raise the dew point to the ambient temperature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/ISS-40_Thunderheads_near_Borneo.jpg/330px-ISS-40_Thunderheads_near_Borneo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloud","wikidata":"Q8074"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Dreamy_Twilight.jpg/500px-Dreamy_Twilight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Dreamy_Twilight.jpg/1280px-Dreamy_Twilight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Dreamy_Twilight.jpg/500px-Dreamy_Twilight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&